      "title": "[P1] Wait for PostgreSQL before seeding",
      "body": "`docker compose up -d` returns once the database container is started, not once its healthcheck passes, so on a cold runner the immediately following seed step can fail with a PostgreSQL connection error before the server is ready. Use Compose's health-wait support or explicitly poll `pg_isready` before invoking the seed script.",
